keywords:
  - analytic number theory
  - Dirichlet L-functions
  - simple zeros
  - critical line
  - large sieve
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
abstract: >-
  Paper, Lean 4 formalisation and verification records. Unconditionally, for a weighted family of
  primitive Dirichlet L-functions, at least 0.9322 − ε of the zeros at polylogarithmic height are simple
  and on the critical line, with explicit bounds up to any fixed polynomial height in the conductor.
  Theorems 1.1 and 1.4(a) are machine-checked in Lean 4.
